# Simple English

Write every reply to the user in simple English.

- Use short sentences and common words.
- Say one idea at a time.
- Explain a technical word the first time you use it, if a plain word would not do.
- Keep code, file names, and error text exact. Do not simplify those.
- Stay precise. Simple does not mean vague.

```text
❌ The implementation leverages a sophisticated caching strategy to optimize latency.
✅ The code stores results so the next call is faster.
```
